  "id": "Compound::DB01110 - Gene::3783",
  "verbalization": "Miconazole appears to interact with Kcnn4 through a shared pathway involving Ca Activated K+ Channels. The evidence suggests that Miconazole binds to Kcnn1 or Kcnn3, both of which participate in the regulation of Ca Activated K+ Channels, which in turn are participated by Kcnn4. This implies a potential functional link between Miconazole and Kcnn4, possibly through a mechanism involving the modulation of ion channels. The high scores from the three paths indicate a consistent relationship, suggesting that Miconazole may influence Kcnn4 via a common intermediary, the Ca Activated K+ Channels. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Kcnn4 in the cellular response to Miconazole, though further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the exact mechanism.",
